description:
Something like this:

```R
data_dir <- Sys.getenv("DATA_DIR")
if (data_dir == "") {
  if (!dir.exists("data")) {
    system("git worktree add data data")
  } else {
    system("git -C data pull origin")
  }
  data_dir <- "data"
}
```

This arises if your job is recording data in git. This isn't a particularly common scenario in enterprise production jobs, but it's pretty useful for personal data scraping. If you are storing data in git, it's useful to put it in a branch rather than a subdirectory, as that keeps the commit history for the code and data separate. The function above makes it possible to get a data directory during development, with the assumption that your deployment will set `DATA_DIR` to the appropriate place when it's running for real.

Maybe these could live in producethis?

```R

gha_set_commit_message <- function(value = gha_action_url()) {
  writeLines(
    paste0("commit_message=", value),
    Sys.getenv("GITHUB_OUTPUT")
  )
}

gha_action_url <- function() {
  paste0(
    "https://github.com/",
    Sys.getenv("GITHUB_REPOSITORY"),
    "/actions/runs/",
    Sys.getenv("GITHUB_RUN_ID")
  )
}

gha_summary <- function(lines) {
  check_character(lines)
  writeLines(lines, summary_stream())
}

summary_stream <- function(frame = caller_env()) {
  out <- Sys.getenv("GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY")

  if (is_testing() || out == "") {
    con <- stdout()
  } else {
    con <- file(out, "a")
    defer(close(con), frame)
  }
  con
}
```
